;; og:preserve-this: do-launch and launch-nearby-players are both flagged as
;; asm by config (decompiler/config/jakx/ntsc_v1/hacks.jsonc, "plow rung
;; (levels-other-tier-3)"). Both inline the same process<->handle sllv/dsra32
;; idiom already parked elsewhere in this tree (rigid-body-queue's own method
;; 10/11/13/15), reading a handle field at an offset (4516 from a net-player
;; pointer for launch-nearby-players' own ragdoll/ownership check, 228 from
;; the other net entity for do-launch's own root lookup) that types2's own
;; ForwardProp pass rejects regardless of what type_casts.jsonc declares for
;; the source register: the "Could not figure out load" throw happens inside
;; types2's own forward propagation, before type_casts.jsonc is ever
;; consulted (type_casts.jsonc only patches the post-hoc conversion back to
;; the old TypeState format, confirmed by reading
;; decompiler/types2/ForwardProp.cpp and decompiler/types2/types2.cpp
;; directly). Every other part of both functions (the *active-net-non-
;; spectators* walk, the net-player-method-49/22 dispatches, the
;; vector-lerp!/vector-normalize! calls) is fully clean, config-fixed
;; evidence, and stays in type_casts.jsonc for the next rung that wants to
;; retry a full decode. do-launch itself has no other landed caller (it is
;; only ever reached from inside launch-nearby-players' own unlanded body),
;; so it gets no extern here; launch-nearby-players is declared below because
;; plow-trans calls it by name.
;; RUNTIME HAZARD: launch-nearby-players links as zero until a real body
;; lands. plow-trans (the shared :trans body for following-path/reverse/
;; intro-path) calls it whenever a plow's own been-hit flag is set, which
;; following-path's own :event handler sets on every 'impact-impulse network
;; message; any plow that takes damage while following-path, reverse or
;; intro-path is active and receives its own :trans dispatch afterward
;; crashes on this call. Not reachable from a default single-player boot
;; (plow only links into ATOPLOW/KCRSPLOW, not GAME.CGO), but reachable the
;; moment a plow is loaded and damaged in an active net game.
(define-extern launch-nearby-players (function none :behavior plow))

